course: dictionary
lesson: 8881
title: Shove and what it means
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words can mean more than one thing, and the sentence tells you which meaning is right. «A Station Road boy shoved Maddie so hard she fell on the kerb and split her lip.» She fell and hurt herself, so shove means push roughly and hard.
explain: Now read «He shoves the tablet under a cushion.» Nobody is being hurt here, so shove means put something somewhere quickly and carelessly. Ask yourself: is someone being pushed, or is something being put away fast?
explain: Shove can also be a noun, a name for a thing. «Give it a shove» means one hard, rough push. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Does it still make sense?
fact: To shove means to push someone or something roughly and hard, or to put something somewhere quickly and carelessly.
fact: A shove is a hard, rough push, as in «give it a shove».
fact: Shove is a verb as well as a noun: shove, shoves, shoved, shoving.
fact: «Shove over» is an informal phrase that means move along to make room.
fact: Teachers say «no pushing or shoving» because shoving in a queue is rude and can hurt someone.
exercise: «A boy shoved Maddie so hard she fell on the kerb.» What does shoved mean here? | Whispered a secret to her | Waved to her from across the road | Hugged her gently | *Pushed roughly and hard
exercise: «He shoves the tablet under a cushion.» What is he doing with the tablet? | Giving it to his teacher | Reading it slowly and carefully | Breaking it with a hard push | *Putting it away quickly and carelessly
exercise: Find and copy the word that tells what the boy in Leeds did to the girl with the hot soup. | ahead | queue | soup | *shoved
test: Which sentence uses shove as a noun? | Sam shoves the door shut. | Ben shoved his coat into his bag. | Maya is shoving her way through the crowd. | *Ella gave the car a shove and it rolled forward.
test: Why do teachers say «no pushing or shoving»? | Because shoving makes the queue move faster | Because shoving means dancing | Because shoving is a sport | *Because shoving can hurt people
exam: Which form of shove is the past tense? | shoves | shoving | a shove | *shoved
